.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt DTFL_DIAG_SESSION_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_diag_session_new ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_session_free ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_server_start ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_server_port ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_server_stop ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_replay_fd ,
.Nm dtfl_diag_replay_fds
.Nd in-process dataflow diagnostics server and log-stream replay
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/diag.h
.Ft dtfl_diag_session *
.Fn dtfl_diag_session_new "dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_diag_session_free "dtfl_diag_session *s"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_start "dtfl_diag_session *s" "const char *iface" "uint16_t port" "dtfl_diag_server **out"
.Ft uint16_t
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_port "const dtfl_diag_server *srv"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_stop "dtfl_diag_server *srv"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fd "int fd" "const char *stream" "dtfl_log_subscriber_fn fn" "void *ctx"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fds "int const *fds" "size_t nfds" "const char *stream" "dtfl_log_subscriber_fn fn" "void *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions are the C port of the dataflow-diag
.Dq diagnostics
crate: a live diagnostics console for timely and differential dataflow.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_diag_session_new
creates a diagnostics session on the worker
.Fa w
and subscribes it to the worker's
.Dq timely
and
.Dq differential/arrange
log streams
.Pq Xr dtfl_worker_log_subscribe 3 .
The session maintains the live set of operators, channels and
statistics.
It is worker-owned: create, use and free it on the worker
thread.
.Fn dtfl_diag_session_free
releases the session; stop any server started from it first.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_start
starts a WebSocket server for the session on interface
.Fa iface
.Pq a NULL Fa iface No means 127.0.0.1
and
.Fa port
.Pq 0 lets the kernel choose .
On success it stores the server in
.Fa *out
and returns
.Dv DTFL_OK ;
on failure it returns a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code with detail in
.Xr dtfl_last_error_detail 3 .
The server runs its accept and send loop on a background thread
.Pq Xr dtfl_set_thread_hooks 3 applies
and communicates with the session through an internal lock-free queue,
so no worker-owned handle crosses the thread boundary.
A browser that connects is replayed the full current state as one
.Em Frame ,
then follows the incremental Frames as the computation runs.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_port
returns the port the server bound.
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_stop
stops the server, joins its thread and frees it; a NULL argument is a
no-op.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fd
and
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fds
replay a recorded log stream and deliver decoded event batches to a
subscriber, the out-of-process counterpart of
.Xr dtfl_worker_log_subscribe 3 .
.Fa stream
names the event enum to decode:
.Dq timely ,
.Dq differential/arrange
or
.Dq communication .
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fd
reads one descriptor to end of stream;
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fds
reads
.Fa nfds
descriptors, one per source worker.
Both return
.Dv DTFL_OK
at clean end of stream, or a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code
.Pq Dv DTFL_EPROTO No on malformed bytes .
.Sh FRAME FORMAT
Each WebSocket text message is one JSON Frame
.Pq PLAN D9, Rust 0.31 compatible :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"type":"Frame","ts_us":<u64>,"updates":[
  {"type":"Operator","id":<u>,"name":"...","addr":[...],"diff":<i64>},
  {"type":"Channel","id":<u>,"scope_addr":[...],
   "source":[<u>,<u>],"target":[<u>,<u>],"diff":<i64>},
  {"type":"Stat","kind":"Elapsed|Messages|...","id":<u>,"diff":<i64>}
]}
.Ed
The upstream
.Pa index.html
and React console render these Frames unmodified.
.Sh DIVERGENCE
The server binds 127.0.0.1 by default, where upstream binds 0.0.0.0
.Pq Pa diagnostics/src/server.rs:154 ,
so operator names and timings are not published to the network with no
authentication
.Pq PLAN D12 .
Pass a different
.Fa iface
to restore the upstream behavior.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_diag_session_new
returns the session, or NULL on a bad argument.
.Fn dtfl_diag_server_start ,
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fd
and
.Fn dtfl_diag_replay_fds
return
.Dv DTFL_OK
or a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl-diag 1 ,
.Xr dtfl_config_log_subscribe 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_log_subscribe 3
.Sh STANDARDS
Ported from differential-dataflow
.Pa diagnostics/src/lib.rs ,
.Pa server.rs
and
.Pa logging.rs
at tag differential-dataflow-v0.25.1.
